The legal texts come from official publications of the Co-operative Republic of Guyana:

  Laws of Guyana, revised editions L.R.O. 1/2012 and L.R.O. 1/2022, and the 2010 consolidation of Cap. 1:01,
  Ministry of Legal Affairs (https://www.mola.gov.gy/laws-of-guyana; earlier editions read from the Internet
  Archive), and Acts of Parliament as published in the Official Gazette (https://parliament.gov.gy),
  retrieved 28 October 2026.

Neither source states a licence. They are official legal texts of Guyana, reproduced with the attribution above;
their copyright status is not confirmed here.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; running heads, marginal notes and Part/Chapter/Title headings were left
out; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the Acts that made each change. The wording of the law
was not changed. Neither the Ministry of Legal Affairs nor the Parliament of Guyana endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
